Yes. Eating a chameleon triggers a _single_ polymorph, for a monster
(pet) just as well as for the player. 

>  Also, is there any way to
> "uncancel" a monster.  My pet Lich would point around and curse alot,
> but was pretty ineffectual at anything other than garnering attention.

The most straightforward way is to kill a creature and resurrect it.
This will get rid of cancellation. 
Of course it's rather unreliable for monsters that only have a
_chance_ to leave a corpse, and it's completely impractical for
liches, who are guaranteed _not_ to leave one: if by chance any
flavour of lich leaves a corpse, the carcass is explicitly destroyed
before it hits the ground. 

So to uncancel your lich, you would have to polymorph it into
something else (difficult, since liches have high magic resistance)
until you get something that can leave a corpse, do the kill-resurrect
trick on that one and _then_ turn it back into a lich. Good luck.

NB: checked this in 3.4.1.; i can't guarantee the uncancellation trick
still works.

